{1041}{Master of Temporal Magick. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1042}{Champion of the Pit on the Isle of Despair.  By defeating all of the pit warriors, you have gained the reputation of being the most grizzled pit fighter of them all.}
{1043}{Instigator of the Orc Riots. You are now considered an enemy not only of Tarant, but Caladon as well. Perhaps more armor is called for.} 
{1044}{Honorary Ambassador to Tarant.  Because of your excellent performance in the negotiations for Caladon's membership in the Unified Kingdom, you are seen as a hero by many of Tarant's citizens.}
{1045}{Enemy of Tulla. You have brought the wrath of every citizen of Tulla upon yourself.}
{1046}{Enemy of T'sen-Ang. Should you enter T'sen-Ang again, you should be prepared for a violent end.}
{1047}{Savior of Bessie Toone. The people of Shrouded Hills have taken a liking to you as the person responsible for freeing the ghost of Bessie Toone.}
{1048}{Destroyer of the Dread Crystal Spider.  For killing the Dread Crystal Spider, you've become a hero in the eyes of the people of the Wheel Clan.}
{1049}{Hero of Shrouded Hills. Because of your heroic efforts in helping Doc Roberts stop the bank robbery, the people of Shrouded Hills are definitely friendlier to you than they once were.}
{1050}{Outlaw of Shrouded Hills. Everyone in Shrouded Hills is looking to kill you for robbing their bank.}
{1051}{Survivor of the crash of the I.F.S. Zephyr. Since selling your story to the Tarantian, it seems some people have begun to recognize you, for better or worse.}
{1052}{Killer of the Whytechurch Murderer. The people of Caladon have taken a liking to you for ridding their city of the dreaded murderer.}
{1053}{Rescuer of Thorvald. Because you have safely returned Thorvald to his clan, the dwarves of the Wheel Clan have taken a liking to you.}
{1054}{Hero of the Wheel Clan. As the person responsible for convincing Loghaire to return to the throne, you have become extremely well liked by members of the Wheel Clan.}
{1055}{Assassin of King Farad. As the killer of the beloved King of Caladon, you will find yourself in grave danger if you were to ever set foot in Caladon again.}
{1056}{Orator of Ashbury. Because of your rousing speech that enabled the townspeople of Ashbury to finally build their monument, you find the people there to be friendlier to you.}
{1057}{Thief of Shrouded Hills. Because of your repeated attempts to steal from the merchants of Shrouded Hills, the merchants and the guards there take a dim view of you and your activities.}
{1058}{Thief of Tarant. Because of your repeated attempts to steal from the merchants of Tarant, the merchants and the guards there take a dim view of you and your activities.}
{1059}{Thief of Ashbury. Because of your repeated attempts to steal from the merchants of Ashbury, the merchants and the guards there take a dim view of you and your activities.}
{1060}{Thief of Black Root. Because of your repeated attempts to steal from the merchants of Black Root, the merchants and the guards there take a dim view of you and your activities.}
{1061}{Thief of Caladon. Because of your repeated attempts to steal from the merchants of Caladon, the merchants and the guards there take a dim view of you and your activities.}
{1062}{Enemy of Shrouded Hills. Because of your cold hearted killing of guards and citizens in Shrouded Hills, you will be attacked on sight if you return there.}
{1063}{Enemy of Tarant. Because of your cold hearted killing of guards and citizens in Tarant, you will be attacked on sight if you return there.}
{1064}{Enemy of Ashbury. Because of your cold hearted killing of guards and citizens in Ashbury, you will be attacked on sight if you return there.}
{1065}{Enemy of Black Root. Because of your cold hearted killing of guards and citizens in Black Root, you will be attacked on sight if you return there.}
{1066}{Enemy of Caladon. Because of your cold hearted killing of guards and citizens in Caladon, you will be attacked on sight if you return there.}
{1067}{Enemy of Dernholm. Because of your cold hearted killing of guards and citizens in Dernholm, you will be attacked on sight if you return there.}
{1068}{Kerghan's Apprentice.  Because you have joined Kerghan, you are despised by most everyone.}
{1069}{Owner of the Bates Mansion. As the purchaser of the famed Bates Mansion, the people of Tarant have slightly more respect for you than they did before.}
{1070}{Liberator of Maug Maulman. Because you killed T'val Nor and broke the spell that was enslaving the Half Ogres of T'sen-Ang, you have earned their friendship, and the enemity of T'sen-Ang.}
{1071}{Winner of the Ancient Game.}
{1072}{Enemy of the Wheel Clan.  For admitting to the murder of Loghaire Thunder Stone, you have become the sworn enemy of every dwarf in the Wheel Clan.}
{1073}{The Most Honored Dialectician in the Known Universe.  Because you have convinced Kerghan to turn from his diabolical plan, you are seen as the most skilled negotiator in the history of Arcanum.}
{1074}{Companion of a Fair Lady. Because the Lady Druella has joined your party, you benefit from a temporary increase in your Beauty and Charisma when dealing with others.}
{1075}{Betrayer of Magnus Shale Fist.  Because you have betrayed the friendship of Magnus Shale Fist, you are his sworn enemy.}
